Per-phase energy budget instrumentation for GIZMO (diagnostic only).

Re-applies the 11-phase gas-energy accounting that was hoisted out of the main line: it reports
the change in total gas energy (thermal + kinetic) across each phase of the timestep, so an energy
error can be localized to a specific stage. Enabled by ENERGY_BUDGET_DIAGNOSTIC, which on the main
line retains only the synchronized-total report (energy_budget_sync_report).

    git apply scripts/energy_budget_phases.patch      # or: git apply -3 for a 3-way merge

WHAT IT FOUND, in the adiabatic wind_singlestar and SN_singlestar tests (both spawning), where
E_kin + E_th equals the injected energy exactly:
  Two large errors of opposite sign, which nearly cancelled:
    - merge_particles_ij discarding the pair's COM-frame KE   ~ -23% of L*t
    - the WAKEUP kick reversal on mid-step demotion           ~ +18% of L*t  (~6% of E_SN)
  Because they cancelled, the default configuration read a healthy-looking ~0.95 of the injected
  total while carrying a large sink and a large source. Fixed by MERGE_SPLIT_CONSERVE_ENERGY and
  WAKEUP_TRUNCATE_STEP_ON_DEMOTION respectively. A residual few percent survives both; it is
  merge-associated but is neither a bookkeeping error nor temporal truncation error -- see
  scripts/merge_energy_diagnostic.patch, which is the instrument for that one.

READ THE OUTPUT WITH CARE -- this is the easiest way to misread it:
  Only phases bracketing an INSTANTANEOUS operation (mergesplit, spawn) are meaningful. A phase
  spanning a drift or kick sums particles sitting at different kick times, which is not a conserved
  quantity, so energy appears to move between such phases with no error present. For an actual
  conservation test use the 'Energy (synced)' line, which reports only when
  All.HighestActiveTimeBin == All.HighestOccupiedTimeBin -- the sole point where Vel and
  InternalEnergy share a clock. Snapshots never satisfy this: io.cc writes Velocities from P[].Vel
  (kick-time) but InternalEnergy from InternalEnergyPred (drift-time).

  Every EB_MARK is collective (one MPI_Allreduce). Marks MUST sit where every rank reaches them --
  outside branch-dependent conditionals -- or the run deadlocks. See EB_SRCA/EB_SPAWN in run.cc and
  EB_PREMERGE/EB_MERGESPLIT in domain.cc, all deliberately hoisted out of their adjacent branches.

